speechtext:
Should not that have been included in the reference to this International Fishery Commission, and have been dealt with as well? I notice in the last part of the resolution the words;
Providing for the bringing into force by proclamation the regulations prepared by the International Fisheries Commission between Great Britain and the United States, now before the House.
I did not understand that these words were before the House. I understood the minister to say, when the orders of the day were called, and in answer to my hon, friend from Selkirk (Mr. Bradbury), that they would be ready in a short time, and that he would be prepared to go over them with my hon. friend.
